[about]
Title=2 - Install and Launch
Intro=The download, the installer's pages, the finish page and its boxes, and FileDir opening by itself.
Setup=The installer is downloaded, and your reader is running.
Homework=Install FileDir and open it from its desktop shortcut.

[step]

Say=The installer is downloaded; Enter opens it. Windows may first ask whether to run a file from the Internet; Alt plus R, Run, answers it.
Key=Enter
Hear=FileDir Setup dialog

[step]

Say=Each page of the installer is a dialog like any other: Tab through it, Enter for Next. The last page is the finish page, with boxes for what else to install -- the screen reader scripts, and mpv, which the Homer Player plays with.
Key=Enter
Hear=Next button

[step]

Say=A box that is ticked will be done; Spacebar changes it. Install means it is not there yet; Update, that a newer one is available; Reinstall, that it is there and current.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Enter on Finish, and FileDir opens by itself on a folder. The desktop shortcut's key, Alt plus Control plus F, opens it from anywhere after that, and brings it forward if it is open already.
Key=Enter
Hear=FileDir, List box

[step]

Say=What the boxes mean. The screen reader scripts give FileDir's own speech its polish; Install when they are not there, Update when a newer set is available, Reinstall when they are current -- the word is the state. mpv is the player behind the Homer Player; the same three words say its state.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The results box after Finish reports each item by name, one line each, and the same summary is saved in the logs folder under your local application data.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Where things went. FileDir is in Program Files; its settings, its Quick folder and its logs are under your local application data, in a folder named FileDir. An update never touches them.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=F11 checks for a newer FileDir and offers to fetch and run it, so the installer is a one-time visit. Alt plus F1 says the version at any time.
Key=F11
Hear=Elevate Version dialog

[step]

Say=Escape. To remove FileDir later, Windows Settings, Apps; your Quick folder and settings stay unless you delete them.
Key=Escape
Hear=FileDir, List box

[step]

Say=FileDir is one instance: Alt plus Control plus F never opens a second copy, it brings the one forward. The window it brings forward is the last folder you were in, with its tags as you left them.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Before the installer, the download. The ReadMe on the project page has one link, FileDir underscore setup dot exe, and F11 inside an installed FileDir fetches the same file; a browser's download is the only time you touch a web page for FileDir.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=A planned misstep. Run the installer while FileDir is open, and it asks you to close it first, by name; close it, press Retry, and the installer carries on. Nothing is half-installed.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=The first run asks nothing. FileDir opens on the folder you were last in -- or on your Documents folder the first time -- and the reader says the folder's name and its count, then the first line.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What the scripts give. With the screen reader scripts installed, the reader's own commands know FileDir's list: the line is read with its marks said as words, tagged and folder, rather than as symbols.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What to try first. Arrow the list, press Enter on a folder, press Backspace to come up, press F1. Five minutes of that, and walk three's keys are half known already.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Updating later is F11 inside FileDir: it compares the installed version with the newest on the project page, says both, and offers to fetch and run the installer; the installer's finish page then shows the same boxes, each saying its state.
Key=F11
Hear=FileDir 5.0 is the newest version. OK button

[step]

Say=Escape. Settings and the Quick folder survive every update; the installer puts the program in Program Files and leaves your local application data alone.
Key=Escape
Hear=FileDir, List box

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I say the key; the reader says what it does.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus F.
Key=
Hear=Open FileDir
